
# Student Performance Analysis

## Project Overview
This project analyzes student performance to identify factors associated
with final exam scores and provide actionable recommendations.

## Tools
- Microsoft Excel
- Pivot Tables
- Pivot Charts
- Slicers
- Excel Formulas
- Data Visualization

## Dataset
The dataset contains 1,000 student records and includes factors such as:
- Study time
- Attendance
- Sleep hours
- Internet access
- Part-time job
- Parental education
- Previous grades
- Final exam scores

## Key Findings
- Average Final Score: 83.5
- 63.8% of students achieved grades A or B.
- Study time showed a moderate positive correlation with final exam scores (r = 0.6).
- Students with internet access scored about 5 points higher on average.
- Students with part-time jobs scored about 3.3 points lower on average.
- Attendance showed a weak positive correlation with final scores (r = 0.3).
- Gender showed almost no meaningful difference in average performance.

## Recommendations
- Encourage students with lower scores to increase their study time.
- Improve internet access for students who currently lack it.
- Provide additional academic support for students with low attendance.
- Consider flexible study support for students who have part-time jobs.

## Dashboard
The interactive Excel dashboard includes:
- Average Final Score
- Total Students
- High Achievement Rate (A & B)
- Study Time vs Final Exam Score
- Previous Grade vs Final Exam Score
- Internet Access comparison
- Part-Time Job comparison
- Interactive slicers
